WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.652
Now we move from organization to quality.

00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:07.797
A dataset can be perfectly structured and still be unsuitable for analysis.

00:00:07.797 --> 00:00:09.832
Quality is contextual.

00:00:09.832 --> 00:00:15.747
Data that is acceptable for a monthly report may be too stale for a real-time dashboard.

00:00:15.747 --> 00:00:18.317
Quality is also evidence-based.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:23.757
An unusual value should be investigated before we automatically delete or replace it.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:28.917
We will use six dimensions and a five-step workflow to reason about quality.

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:33.217
In practice, quality rules should be tied to a use case.

00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:39.642
A fifteen-minute delay may be acceptable for a monthly report but unacceptable for a real-time alert.

00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:47.532
Likewise, an unusual physiological value should often be flagged and investigated rather than automatically

00:00:47.532 --> 00:00:51.194
deleted. Good cleaning preserves evidence and documents uncertainty.
